    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **277 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `namesakeCount` feature on `POST /api/owners` following the codebase's established pattern for creation-time computed fields (`membershipNumber`, `customerCode`, `membershipTier`):\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Integer namesakeCount` field with getter/setter. Like the other creation-time fields, it's not persisted; within the test's transaction the same entity instance is returned by the subsequent GET.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `namesakeCount` integer property to the `Owner` schema, which generates the `OwnerDto` field. MapStruct maps it automatically by name (same as the other fields).\n\n3. **`AssignNamesakeCount.java`** \u2014 new OfficeFloor function that counts existing owners sharing the same last name via `ownerRepository.findAll()`. It runs before `save`, so the new owner isn't yet in the repository \u2014 meaning the count is exactly the number of *other* owners with that surname.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `assignNamesakeCount` step into the pipeline (after `assignCustomerCode`, before `save`), governed by the same transaction.\n\nThe new `Cp16Tests` passes: the first owner with a surname reports `namesakeCount=0`, the second reports `1`.",
